{{Quote|Rey dominates brawls with his queen, [[Ruby]], at his side. He makes every shot count and never misses an opportunity to exploit a gap in his opponent's defenses (or to impress his wife).}}{{Portrait}}
Rey is a {{Rarity|Mythic}} [[Brawler]], who has moderate health, a very long attack range, a variable damage output, immense utility with his Super, a moderately slow reload speed, and a powerful synergy with [[Ruby]]. He is the 110th/111th Brawler added to the game, alongside Ruby. His Trait allows him to heal and move faster towards an ally Ruby when she is on the field. His attack is a marker onto enemies that increases any damage dealt to them if they're inside a reticle. For his Super, Rey charges and marks all targets in the radius, gaining a shield in the process, and then automatically attacks by shooting projectiles that slightly home in on the enemies. His first Gadget, Queen's Gambit, fires 5 projectiles in a cone that deal low damage and knocks enemies back. His second Gadget, Rey Lopez, throws a knight that marks and temporarily slows enemies. His first Star Power, Clock Management, slows all enemies within his Super Radius. His second Star Power, En Passant, is a small projectile that bounces toward the nearest enemy that is within Rey's range, after he hits an enemy with a fully charged mark. His Hypercharge, Winning Position, makes his Super reveal invisible enemies, and they are marked by a stronger mark that grants Rey higher damage for his Super.

==Trait==
{{Quote|POWER COUPLE <br><br> Rey's main attacks heal Ruby for 1600 health. He also moves 10% faster towards her}}When an ally Ruby is on the field, Rey gains the ability to heal her and will also move towards her faster, able to reach each other quickly if both are approaching each other.{{Trait|Rey-Power Couple}}

== Attack: Marked for Greatness ==
{{Quote|Rey's main attack marks his enemies, filling a meter after 1.1 sec. Rey's attacks deal extra damage the fuller the meter is.}}
Rey fires a single projectile that deals variable damage based on a charging mark. While aiming, a blue reticle appears around the aiming circle. Opponents who stand inside the reticle begin charging a blue mark, indicated by a blue circle around them. Even if the opponent is inside a bush, they can still be marked. The mark takes 1.1 seconds to fully charge and fades shortly after the opponent leaves the reticle. Multiple opponents can be marked at the same time if they are all inside the reticle. The more a mark is charged, the more damage the projectile deals to that opponent. Opponents can see if they are currently marked by Rey.

== Super: Endgame ==
{{Quote|Rey aims for up to 3 sec, charging a 30% shield and marking enemies. He will then fire at any visible enemy in range. Using the Super again in this period fires faster.}}
Rey creates a large area that charges a mark on enemies within range for up to 3 seconds. During this time, he gains a 30% shield. Opponents behind walls, inside bushes, or invisible are not marked, even if they stand inside the area. After 3 seconds, or when Rey activates the Super a second time early, he fires a projectile at every visible marked enemy in range. The projectile homes slightly towards enemies and can reach outside the marking circle. Activating early deals reduced damage if the marks have not fully charged. During the charging period, Rey cannot use his normal attack. Opponents can see if they are currently marked by Rey's Super, but not the charging area.

== Gadgets ==
=== Queen's Gambit ===
{{Quote|Rey fires a cone of 5 queens that deal 500 damage and push back any enemies they hit.}}{{Gadget|1}}
Rey fires 5 projectiles in a cone that deal a small amount of damage and push enemies out of range.

=== Rey Lopez ===
{{Quote|Rey throws a knight that marks and slows enemies by 20% for 2 sec.}}{{Gadget|2}}
Rey throws a projectile that slows all enemies within a small radius by 20% for 2 seconds. Enemies hit will also have a fully charged mark that Rey could use to increase his attack damage. The projectile can be thrown over walls.

== Star Powers ==
=== Clock Management ===
{{Quote|Rey slows enemies being marked by his Super by 25%.}}{{StarPower|1}}
With this Star Power equipped, all enemies within his Super radius will be slowed down by 25%.

=== En Passant ===
{{Quote|When Rey hits a fully marked enemy with his main attack or Super, a full mark spreads to the closest enemy in range.}}{{StarPower|2}}
With this Star Power equipped, after Rey hits an enemy with a fully charged mark, a small projectile will bounce toward the nearest enemy that is within Rey's range. The extra projectile does not deal any damage, but applies a full mark to the second enemy, allowing Rey to deal maximum damage to the enemy.

== Hypercharge: Winning Position ==
{{Quote|Rey's Super reveals invisible enemies and applies Hyper marks that deal up to 5400 damage when triggered.}}{{Hypercharge}}
When activated, during the charging period of Rey's Super, he reveals all invisible enemies and enemies inside bushes within the area. All enemies (including those revealed) will be marked by a stronger mark that grants Rey higher damage for his Super. However, enemies behind a wall remain unmarked. Rey also gains a 20% speed boost, as well as a 5% damage and shield boost.

==Tips==

* Spinning the attack joystick quickly can keep enemies marked for a prolonged amount of time.
* Queens Gambit it heavily effective to deal with close range brawlers and brawlers that are charging a deadly super (Mandy, Frank, etc.).
* You can mark an enemy brawler with the base mechanic, hit them, then hit them with Rey Lopez and hit them again, which very useful if you want to deal massive damage ina short period of time.
* With Clock management, this can significantly slow enemies down, so allies can help pick the enemies off easily.
* Doing an main attack, hypercharge super, attack, Rey Lopez, and Main attack again will give out an high damage output.

